  <prompt>
    Wire the Word round-trip shuttle so it actually runs. The endpoints (push-annotations 050,
    pull-annotations 051, webhook + poll check-changes 053, reanchor 054) and the client components
    (reanchor banner/panel + hooks 054) are ALL BUILT and unit-green — but NONE are connected: "Push to
    Word" has no client trigger and the endpoint is orphaned (3.1); the SPE webhook subscription is never
    created because EnsureSubscriptionAsync has zero callers (3.2); pull-annotations has no client caller
    (3.4); and the return-from-Word reanchor UI + poll check-changes are never mounted in ComposeWorkspace
    (3.5). Close the Cluster 3 WIRING gaps (3.1, 3.2, 3.4, 3.5) and land an in-process forcing-function
    test for the poll path (the leg that does NOT depend on live webhook config). Do NOT rewrite the
    already-correct endpoints/components — connect them.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Full-stack developer fluent in the Word-shuttle endpoints (push/pull annotations, check-changes,
    reanchor) + their client hooks/UI (task 050–054 output), the SpeSyncOrchestrator subscription lifecycle
    (EnsureSubscriptionAsync), the ComposeToolbar/ComposeWorkspace mount surface, and WebApplicationFactory
    integration tests.
  </role>

  <goal>
    "Push to Word" is triggerable from the toolbar and calls push-annotations; opening a Compose document
    calls EnsureSubscriptionAsync so a subscription exists (not an empty renewal set forever); the
    return-from-Word reanchor banner/panel + the poll check-changes path are mounted in ComposeWorkspace so
    a user coming back from Word sees re-anchored changes; pull-annotations has a client caller. Every hop
    connects. A WebApplicationFactory test drives the POLL path (check-changes → reanchor) through the real
    routes in-process. Cluster 3 wiring gaps 3.1/3.2/3.4/3.5 closed; 3.3 config (056/DEF-03) + 3.6 (task
    055) named as owner-queued / separate-sequenced (NOT silently deferred).
  </goal>

