  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Load the register Cluster 3 + this POML + defer-issues DEF-03. Confirm the 050–054 endpoints + 054 reanchor components exist and are correct (they are — wire, don't rebuild). Find the Compose document-load path (for the EnsureSubscriptionAsync origin call) and the ComposeToolbar/ComposeWorkspace mount points.</step>
    <step order="1">Push-to-Word (gap 3.1): add the toolbar action calling the existing push-annotations endpoint.</step>
    <step order="2">Subscription origin call (gap 3.2): invoke EnsureSubscriptionAsync on Compose document load so a subscription is created (not an empty renewal set). Keep it within the SpeSyncOrchestrator facade.</step>
    <step order="3">Pull caller (gap 3.4): add the pull-annotations client caller reusing the 051 pattern.</step>
    <step order="4">Reanchor mount + poll (gap 3.5): mount the 054 reanchor banner/panel in ComposeWorkspace and wire the POLL check-changes path (poll-on-focus) as the change signal (webhook delivery stays owner-config-gated). Typed bus discriminants only.</step>
    <step order="5">ANTI-RECURRENCE TEST (definition-of-done, non-waivable): add ComposeWordShuttlePollEndpointContractTests — a WebApplicationFactory test driving the POLL path (check-changes → reanchor) through the real routes in-process, asserting a detected change reanchors. (The webhook-delivery leg is ✅◐ E2E-pending on task 056 config — state that.)</step>
    <step order="6">Verify: dotnet build + dotnet test (new + Compose regression); Compose.Components tsc + jest; publish-size + CVE. Run Step 9.5 (code-review + adr-check) UNCONDITIONALLY. Update this POML notes. NAME task 056 (webhook config) + task 055 (deterministic orchestration) as the remaining sequenced/owner items. Do NOT edit TASK-INDEX/current-task (main session reconciles).</step>
  </steps>

